# Code Quality Principles

**Prioritize Readability:** Keeping functions small makes code easier to audit, even if you don't hit the exact 60-line limit.

**Favor the Compiler:** As noted by developers, if you can write code that the compiler can verify (avoiding ambiguous logic), do it! Using modern static analysis tools can catch bugs before they reach production.

**Defensive Programming:** The practice of checking all return values and being explicit about your intent is a great habit for any developer looking to write cleaner, safer code.